# WordPress taxonomy paths, for the rck-pm.com content when it lands here.
# NOTE: the spec's "/post/* -> /insights/:splat" rule is deliberately absent.
# /post/<slug> is this site's live canonical blog URL — 12 posts were migrated
# off Wix at exactly those addresses so no redirect was needed. That rule would
# 301 every live post to /insights/<slug>, which does not exist.
/category/*                  /insights                                       301!
/author/*                    /about/team                                     301!

# ── Unmatched paths get a real 404 ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Previously this was "/*  /index.html  200", which answered every URL on the
# domain with the app shell and HTTP 200 — a soft 404. Crawlers read that as
# "infinite valid pages", which wastes crawl budget and can suppress the real
# ones. Safe to make strict because every router page is prerendered to a real
# file: scripts/prerender.mjs ROUTES and the ROUTES map in src/App.jsx are in
# sync (30 each, verified), and blog posts are added from disk. If you add a
# page to App.jsx, add it to prerender.mjs too or it will now hard-404.
